otection and a subsequent multirow veto reject them. The 60 field bands and seven additions are not evidence that these old fixes survived.","owner_words":"> missed lines between 67, 75\n> \n> missed start of lines from 75, up to 103\n> also between 41 and 44","page":"s2-49598b2e848ab1f0ee1e-p00001","r7_status":"partly","status":"no_unambiguous_region; two-catalogue evidence only"},{"bindings":[],"comment_id":"R4-57","crop_ids":[],"failure_types":["curl_end_cut","multi_line_segment"],"observation":"Column crossings are cut; seven real text pieces are recovered and 17 field bands follow the right bend. Some right-end words remain detached or outside the bands, and some neighbouring straight crops still cross rows.","owner_words":"> there is a column boundary in the middle which is ignored completely and the lines are unified.\n> \n> also many lines are missed here, but none are added\n> \n> also there is curvature to teh right and some chars at ends of lines are missed","page":"s2-49598b2e848ab1f0ee1e-p00004","r7_status":"partly","status":"no_unambiguous_region; two-catalogue evidence only"},{"bindings":[],"comment_id":"R4-63","crop_ids":[],"failure_types":["missed_line"],"observation":"Regression against task C: the recovered name row at y=712–801 is mostly absent (12,558 of 13,696 old owned ink pixels uncovered). The changed regional detection hits the existing multirow-height veto. Other field bands improve the bend, but broad straight boxes and detached starts remain.","owner_words":"> missed 2 lines between 9 and 10","page":"s2-3229200bf47ca465a42d-p00004","r7_status":"partly","status":"no_unambiguous_region; two-catalogue evidence only"},{"bindings":[],"comment_id":"R4-71","crop_ids":[],"failure_types":["curl_end_cut"],"observation":"Seven native join groups and three recovered pieces remain. All field proposals are vetoed, so internal omissions and severe curled right ends remain unresolved.","owner_words":"> missed line content internally between 1 and 8 (horizontal)\n> \n> and also missed lines between 15 and 16\n> and also 2 below 57\n> \n> also many words missed to the right of lines as page curves to the right","page":"s2-86865c33eef5932c013b-p00005","r7_status":"partly","status":"no_unambiguous_region; two-catalogue evidence only"},{"bindings":[],"comment_id":"R4-72","crop_ids":[],"failure_types":["multi_line_segment","fragment_crop"],"observation":"Columns are separated, 16 segments are recovered and 31 field bands follow the left bend. Several marked rows are now isolated; other crops remain multirow or include clipped strips. The added-row shape improves locally but smooth segments are not universal.","owner_words":"> there is a column boundary in the middle which is ignored completely and the lines are unified.\n> \n> also many lines are missed here, but none are added\n> \n> there is curvature to the left\n> \n> the added line is not smooth enough and very close to the chars","page":"s2-49598b2e848ab1f0ee1e-p00005","r7_status":"partly","status":"no_unambiguous_region; two-catalogue evidence only"},{"bindings":[],"comment_id":"R4-73","crop_ids":[],"failure_types":["curl_end_cut"],"observation":"Three recovered pieces, three joins and 13 field bands help selected rows. Severe right-end words remain uncovered; the field does not solve the whole curl.","owner_words":"> curvature to the right, and many last chars are missed","page":"s2-86865c33eef5932c013b-p00007","r7_status":"partly","status":"no_unambiguous_region; two-catalogue evidence only"}]
